                       &T         &mut T     *const T   *mut T     Box<T>     Rc<T>
owns (drops) pointee   no         no         no         no         yes        last one
write through it       no         yes        no         in unsafe  if mut     if unique
Copy                   yes        no         yes        yes        no         no
deref needs unsafe     no         no         yes        yes        no         no
can be null            no         no         yes        yes        no         no
pointee may live       anywhere   anywhere   anywhere   anywhere   heap       heap
P<u8>, words           1          1          1          1          1          1
P<[u8]>, words         2          2          2          2          2          2
P<str>, words          2          2          2          2          2          2
P<dyn Display>, words  2          2          2          2          2          2
Option<P<u8>>, words   1          1          2          2          1          1

How each row was filled
  owns       destructor runs when the pointer's scope ends:
             &T 0, &mut T 0, *const T 0, *mut T 0, Box<T> 1;
             Rc<T> 0 after dropping one of two clones, 1 after the last
  write      *m = 2 -> n = 2   unsafe { *q = 3 } -> n = 3   let mut b ...; *b = 4 -> *b = 4
             Rc::get_mut wrote 5 while unique; None after one clone: true
  Copy       controls for the probe: i32 true, String false
  deref      *at_local + *boxed + *counted = 13, outside any unsafe block
  null       yes where None needs a word of its own; std::ptr::null::<u8>().is_null() = true
  lives      one type, &i32, at a local 1, at a static 7, inside a Box 4
  words      size_of::<P>() / size_of::<usize>(), P being the pointer in that column
